WEBVTT

00:02.040 --> 00:04.160
Man, am I bored.

00:05.160 --> 00:07.940
Why can't Kayoko ever leave work on time?

00:11.920 --> 00:12.980
What's taking you so long, Kayoko—

00:12.980 --> 00:14.480
Oh what the hell, it's Vamp.

00:14.480 --> 00:15.110
Shut up.

00:15.110 --> 00:16.940
Why <i>would </i> I be happy to hear from you?

00:16.940 --> 00:19.210
We're fighting tomorrow, aren't we?

00:19.210 --> 00:20.210
Plastic models?

00:20.210 --> 00:21.570
Yeah, I like them.

00:21.570 --> 00:22.500
Bring it over then.

00:22.500 --> 00:24.880
You might be surprised at how good I am with my hands.

00:24.880 --> 00:26.060
Here it is.

00:26.060 --> 00:26.800
It's freakin' huge!

02:00.200 --> 02:01.770
It's a Plastic MODEMO!

02:01.770 --> 02:05.170
I bet you've never made one this big, Mr. Red.

02:05.570 --> 02:07.930
Why did you put tape here?

02:07.930 --> 02:08.870
That's actually...

02:09.270 --> 02:11.780
This is yet another surprising mechanism produced by Florsheim!

02:13.710 --> 02:15.010
So,

02:15.010 --> 02:16.910
you want <i>me </i> to build <i>this?</i>

02:17.010 --> 02:18.130
Yes.

02:18.730 --> 02:20.480
I see you tried to build it already.

02:21.080 --> 02:22.220
Yes.

02:22.220 --> 02:24.740
You gave up on it and brought it to me, then.

02:24.740 --> 02:27.400
I guess I'm good at cooking,

02:27.400 --> 02:29.690
but not so good at making these things.

02:29.690 --> 02:31.920
Then you should get better at it, punk!

02:31.920 --> 02:33.820
That was a good impression of Antkiller, just now.

02:33.820 --> 02:34.650
What?

02:34.650 --> 02:35.750
N-Nothing.

02:35.750 --> 02:37.970
Why couldn't you make one of your youngins do it?

02:37.970 --> 02:40.160
There's gotta be at least one monster that's good at building plastic models.

02:40.160 --> 02:41.190
Well actually,

02:41.190 --> 02:43.240
there's a retreat going on over at HQ,

02:43.240 --> 02:45.910
and all the other monsters were busy working,

02:45.910 --> 02:48.080
so Tiser was all I had to go with.

02:48.480 --> 02:52.020
You're my only hope, Mr. Red!

02:52.020 --> 02:53.460
That's where you're wrong!

02:53.460 --> 02:56.640
But isn't it the Hero's duty to help those in need?

02:56.640 --> 02:58.030
It's to help "those" in need,

02:58.030 --> 03:00.050
not to help "evil organizations" in need!

03:00.050 --> 03:01.640
Also if you apply that logic,

03:01.640 --> 03:03.850
us Heroes would have to do other menial stuff like unclogging toilets

03:03.850 --> 03:05.480
and helping people cross the street!

03:05.480 --> 03:08.780
But you helped us fix the circuit breakers over at the base last time.

03:08.780 --> 03:11.500
That's exactly the kind of "help" that shouldn't be happening!

03:11.500 --> 03:15.510
Please, I just want to get this ready before our battle with Mr. Red tomorrow!

03:15.510 --> 03:17.320
Do you not realize who you're talking to?

03:17.320 --> 03:19.780
All you have to do with the circuit board is load it in like a cassette,

03:19.780 --> 03:21.240
so it should be really easy!

03:21.240 --> 03:23.180
You guys do it then, if it's so simple.

03:25.990 --> 03:27.730
Can you pass me "that", Tiser?

03:27.730 --> 03:29.150
Which? That?

03:29.150 --> 03:30.730
That's the number ten, silly.

03:30.730 --> 03:32.060
I need the number five.

03:32.060 --> 03:33.360
Five, five!

03:33.360 --> 03:35.130
Go home! Do it at your own home!

03:35.130 --> 03:36.900
I don't have time!

03:36.900 --> 03:40.200
I have to submit a report to HQ tomorrow

03:40.200 --> 03:42.420
explaining that you and this robot actually engaged in combat!

03:42.420 --> 03:44.650
This is a matter of life and death for me!

03:44.650 --> 03:45.590
I don't care, just go home!

03:46.000 --> 03:48.430
I'll go home if Kayoko tells me to.

03:48.430 --> 03:49.650
Y-You son of a...

03:49.650 --> 03:50.760
I'm home.

03:53.920 --> 03:56.130
Are you sure you don't want any dinner, Vamp?

03:56.830 --> 03:59.050
Yeah I'll be fine. Thanks Kayoko.

03:59.050 --> 04:00.330
Why don't you help him?

04:00.330 --> 04:04.040
Why do I have to make a robot that's designed to kill me?

04:05.000 --> 04:07.620
You're putting that in upside-down.

04:07.720 --> 04:10.170
I also took a peek at the instruction manual,

04:10.170 --> 04:13.270
and that thing really isn't all that different from a normal plastic model besides its size.

04:13.270 --> 04:14.900
You'd have to be pretty thickheaded to not be able to build it.

04:16.760 --> 04:19.620
Why couldn't HQ have just sent over a pre-built one?

04:19.620 --> 04:21.600
Oh, we're blaming HQ now, are we?

04:24.360 --> 04:27.190
I'd help you if I knew how those things worked.

04:27.190 --> 04:31.040
You should just worry yourself with resting after a hard day's work, Kayoko.

04:31.040 --> 04:33.770
You're making a big mistake if you think I'd crack down and help

04:33.770 --> 04:38.110
just because you look like you're having so much trouble.

04:41.150 --> 04:42.370
Sorry, Vamp,

04:42.370 --> 04:45.140
but I have to be up early tomorrow so I'm going to head on to bed.

04:45.440 --> 04:46.530
Oh, good night.

04:48.730 --> 04:50.790
Shouldn't you be helping them?

04:53.260 --> 04:54.730
And you're sleeping.

04:55.030 --> 04:56.480
Wake up, you.

04:57.080 --> 04:58.160
Geez.

05:00.730 --> 05:02.570
It doesn't fit...

05:04.860 --> 05:06.590
Where are the parts I need?

05:06.590 --> 05:08.740
Five, five!

05:12.950 --> 05:14.670
Five...

05:20.680 --> 05:22.420
Oh no, I fell asleep!

05:22.720 --> 05:24.060
A blanket?

05:27.920 --> 05:30.610
I knew you were really a nice guy inside!

05:30.610 --> 05:32.560
Dumbass, Vamp's right outside!

05:32.560 --> 05:33.880
Go back to your side.

05:34.280 --> 05:35.660
Wow!

05:35.660 --> 05:39.370
This is almost like that fairytale where the fairies make shoes for you while you sleep!

05:39.370 --> 05:41.050
I can't believe this guy.

05:41.050 --> 05:41.720
Five!

05:42.780 --> 05:44.260
Nozawana!

05:44.260 --> 05:47.110
It was you who built the robot, right, Mr. Red?

05:47.110 --> 05:49.290
No shit, who else could have done it?

05:49.290 --> 05:51.580
Would you like seconds, Mr. Hero?

05:51.580 --> 05:54.180
I'm tired so let's get the fighting over with now.

05:54.180 --> 05:56.180
I wanna get it done quick so I can come back and go back to sleep.

05:56.180 --> 05:56.770
Sure.

05:56.770 --> 05:58.380
But you see...

05:58.380 --> 06:02.540
You just might never wake up again after today.

06:02.540 --> 06:05.680
I really want to open up this guy's head and see what's inside.

06:08.870 --> 06:09.820
That's strange.

06:13.460 --> 06:14.840
What now?

06:14.840 --> 06:16.710
This can't be right,

06:16.710 --> 06:18.120
the switch is on, but...

06:18.120 --> 06:20.460
It couldn't have been me; I followed the instructions perfectly.

06:20.460 --> 06:22.230
Something must be wrong with the circuit.

06:22.230 --> 06:23.490
Let me see it.

06:23.490 --> 06:24.440
Please do!

06:25.040 --> 06:26.690
Master Vamp!

06:26.990 --> 06:28.860
Number One, Number Two!

06:28.860 --> 06:30.340
Did you get my voicemail?

06:30.340 --> 06:33.190
Yes, we came straight from the retreat without stopping by the base first,

06:33.190 --> 06:35.950
so we couldn't bring you your spear and shield like you asked.

06:36.450 --> 06:38.080
Is the fight over already?

06:38.080 --> 06:39.190
Not yet.

06:39.190 --> 06:42.420
Something's wrong with the robot, so Mr. Red's taking a look at it for us.

06:42.420 --> 06:44.240
What the hell, you plugged this in the wrong way!

06:44.240 --> 06:46.000
Did you find out what's wrong with it?

06:46.000 --> 06:50.280
"Just load it in like a cassette," my ass.

06:50.580 --> 06:51.970
This should do it.

06:51.970 --> 06:54.500
Here we go for real this time!

06:54.500 --> 06:55.260
All right!

06:59.480 --> 07:00.460
It moved!

07:01.460 --> 07:03.270
What the, it stopped.

07:03.610 --> 07:04.780
What now?

07:04.780 --> 07:06.260
Didn't you hear it go "snap" too?

07:06.260 --> 07:06.970
I'm not sure...

07:06.970 --> 07:09.180
One of the circuits in his arm must have fried.

07:10.120 --> 07:11.100
Found it.

07:11.100 --> 07:12.980
The coupler fell out, see?

07:13.880 --> 07:15.570
What should we do?

07:15.570 --> 07:17.190
What's a coupler, by the way?

07:17.190 --> 07:19.640
This cable harness is too short.

07:19.640 --> 07:22.540
Run over to the electronics strore and get me a longer one of these for me.

07:22.540 --> 07:23.990
A longer one, right?

07:23.990 --> 07:25.610
It's gotta be around 50cm, okay?

07:25.610 --> 07:27.610
You should be writing this down, Vamp.

07:27.610 --> 07:29.330
You're supposed to submit a report afterwards, right?

07:29.330 --> 07:29.990
Oh yeah.

07:39.340 --> 07:40.260
All right!

07:44.030 --> 07:45.210
It's showtime!

07:56.870 --> 07:59.450
Go prepare me another robot, come on!

07:59.450 --> 08:01.310
You've awakened the craftsman's spirit in me now.

08:01.310 --> 08:04.510
I won't rest easy until I've fought a robot built with my own hands!

08:04.510 --> 08:07.160
Like I said, that was only an experimental product.

08:07.160 --> 08:09.470
You're going to take the lazy way out after all you've done?

08:09.470 --> 08:11.600
He's surprisingly good with his hands.

08:11.600 --> 08:13.380
Astro Fighter Sunred.

08:13.380 --> 08:15.540
This is the magnificent story of the conflict between good and evil

08:15.540 --> 08:18.570
that takes place in the city of Kawasaki.

08:18.570 --> 08:19.980
Five, five.

08:24.600 --> 08:24.970
Punk!

08:25.370 --> 08:26.770
*Buzz*

08:33.130 --> 08:34.680
Cheers!

08:34.680 --> 08:37.260
Thanks for your hard work!

08:37.760 --> 08:39.180
Damn it.

08:39.180 --> 08:42.400
I could have kicked Red's ass if I had molted.

08:42.400 --> 08:43.640
That's so true.

08:43.640 --> 08:47.350
We're so sorry we called you out to fight right before you were supposed to molt.

08:47.350 --> 08:49.440
Antkiller suddenly came down with a stomach ache.

08:49.440 --> 08:50.890
These things happen.

08:50.890 --> 08:53.840
I've had others fill in for me too, so I'm just paying back the favor.

08:53.840 --> 08:55.840
You're so mature about it.

08:55.840 --> 08:57.690
I have one order of stone pot bibimbap and cold buckwheat noodles,

08:57.690 --> 09:00.330
and a side of pickled cucumbers for you guys.

08:59.560 --> 09:00.730
Pass me the buckwheat noodles.

09:00.730 --> 09:02.090
I got the stone pot bibimbap.

09:02.090 --> 09:02.820
Here you are.

09:02.820 --> 09:05.640
Are you sure you're okay with just the cucumbers, Mr. Cicadanga?

09:05.640 --> 09:07.990
This is like a dinner for us, actually.

09:07.990 --> 09:11.890
Oh, I had two bananas before the fight, so I'm good.

09:11.890 --> 09:13.260
Ah I see.

09:13.260 --> 09:17.730
I have to finish off the udon I made this morning when I get back too.

09:17.730 --> 09:19.500
Do you cook, Mr. Cicadanga?

09:19.500 --> 09:20.870
Oh no.

09:20.870 --> 09:25.430
It's one of those those pre-made ones in the aluminum package that you just pour the sauce in and boil.

09:25.430 --> 09:27.560
I hardly ever cook.

09:27.560 --> 09:29.670
Yeah, those things are delicious.

09:30.220 --> 09:32.440
But even with the bananas you ate,

09:32.440 --> 09:34.790
are you sure the leftover udon will be enough?

09:34.790 --> 09:37.330
Oh, after I'm done with the udon,

09:37.330 --> 09:41.490
I usually put in one of those pre-cooked rice packages into the leftover soup.

09:41.890 --> 09:43.160
I do that too.

09:43.160 --> 09:45.810
Yeah, it almost tastes better than the udon itself.

09:45.810 --> 09:48.980
The tempura crumbs make it so much more worth it.

09:49.480 --> 09:51.050
You got that right.

09:55.020 --> 09:56.810
I'm gonna get going.

09:56.810 --> 09:59.360
Yeah, see you at tomorrow's meeting.

09:59.360 --> 10:00.690
Oh, the reflection meeting, right?

10:02.710 --> 10:04.200
I'll be there, don't worry.

10:04.200 --> 10:05.010
Laters.

10:06.010 --> 10:07.780
Damn it.

10:08.000 --> 10:12.160
I could have kicked Red's ass if I had molted.

10:12.160 --> 10:13.250
Wait,

10:13.250 --> 10:15.750
he didn't give us enough money.

10:15.750 --> 10:17.280
Don't say that.

10:17.280 --> 10:18.680
It's Mr. Cicadanga we're talking about here.

10:20.780 --> 10:22.950
I guess you're right.

10:24.350 --> 10:25.590
Now that you mention it,

10:25.590 --> 10:28.230
Mr. Cicadanga's been in this business for twenty years, right?

10:28.230 --> 10:29.270
He's a veteran, isn't he.

10:30.650 --> 10:33.320
I wonder what he's going to do after all this.

10:33.320 --> 10:35.440
He keeps saying he's going to molt someday,

10:35.440 --> 10:37.480
but I wonder if he ever will.

10:41.520 --> 10:42.570
Excuse me,

10:42.570 --> 10:43.660
can I get some grapefruit juice?

10:43.660 --> 10:44.340
Sure thing.

10:44.340 --> 10:45.670
You're not going to drink more?

10:45.670 --> 10:48.490
I'm probably going to get sleepy if I drink more.

10:48.490 --> 10:50.090
I can't do that today.

10:50.320 --> 10:52.700
I'm actually going on a date tomorrow,

10:52.700 --> 10:54.140
so I gotta go try on some clothes at home.

10:54.840 --> 10:55.890
Wait, for real?

10:55.890 --> 10:58.550
Yeah, so you really haven't found a girlfriend since that time?

10:58.550 --> 10:59.900
Yeah.

10:59.900 --> 11:01.940
Lucky you, going on dates and everything.

11:01.940 --> 11:04.020
What? Say it louder.

11:04.020 --> 11:05.230
Lucky you!

11:05.230 --> 11:06.320
I still can't hear you.

11:06.320 --> 11:07.670
I said, lucky you, going on dates!

11:07.670 --> 11:08.730
I can't hear you, man!

11:08.730 --> 11:09.620
You're going on a date, huh?

11:09.620 --> 11:11.920
Yeah, it's actually kinda annoying.

11:11.920 --> 11:13.530
Yeah, right.

11:13.530 --> 11:17.210
Oh yeah, why don't you just wear that jacket you bought at BEAMS the other time?

11:17.210 --> 11:18.570
I can't.

11:18.570 --> 11:23.000
She wants to go to the BEAMS over at Takashimaya for our date tomorrow.

11:23.570 --> 11:25.420
I guess you shouldn't wear that then.

11:25.420 --> 11:26.940
Can you imagine how dorky I'd look?

11:29.420 --> 11:31.710
You'd be wearing a jacket inside of BEAMS which you bought at BEAMS,

11:31.710 --> 11:32.800
and that jacket's from this season too.

11:32.800 --> 11:35.210
It's probably still on display in the store.

11:36.350 --> 11:38.330
Wait, what's the date today again?

11:39.430 --> 11:41.020
It's the 23rd.

11:41.420 --> 11:42.520
The 23rd?

11:42.520 --> 11:44.470
Holy shit, my date is supposed to be today!

11:44.770 --> 11:47.730
A peaceful everyday life follows their tumultuous fighting days;

11:47.730 --> 11:49.340
Astro Fighter Sunred.

11:49.340 --> 11:52.380
This is the story of the conflict between good and evil

11:52.380 --> 11:54.940
which takes place in the city of Kanagawa.
